<%# "Connect an AI assistant" (design spec §6.1, round 3): see `_screen`. The
    create form is a plain, non-Turbo POST (`data-turbo="false"`): the one-time
    reveal is a rendered (200) response -- a Drive form submission must
    redirect, and a frame submission leaves Turbo's snapshot cache free to
    keep the reveal for Back -- so it arrives as its own document whose head
    opts out of Turbo's cache (see admin/api_tokens/create). A refused create
    re-renders this very page at 422 (no token exists, so nothing secret).
    Revoke is gated behind `Admin::Ui::ConfirmDialogComponent`, like every other
    destructive action in CS Studio. %>
<% content_for :title, "AI assistant" %>
<%= render "admin/api_tokens/screen", raw_token: nil %>
